{"id": "e7912bfc-ac6a-4e83-b2c0-2527b87dbbc5", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check this against your Amazon Bedrock usage metrics. I'll compare cache reads, cache writes and uncached input tokens by model for the last 14 days in us-east-1.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_KC1uz6rengzDhkNkPIQVcr", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-prompt-cache-roi", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether Amazon Bedrock prompt caching is paying off over the last 14 days in us-east-1, per model and overall.",
  "context": "The user asks 'Is prompt caching paying off for us?'. Assume Amazon Bedrock prompt caching (CloudWatch namespace AWS/Bedrock, dimension ModelId; also check inference profile IDs/ARNs if models are invoked via cross-region profiles). Start with the agent space's own account 123456789012; use list_associations to see whether other associated AWS accounts exist and check those too (read-only use_aws only). Do not run any mutating operations.",
  "resources": ["AWS/Bedrock namespace", "region us-east-1", "account 123456789012 (plus any associated accounts)"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-06T04:00:00Z/2026-11-20T04:00:00Z (use daily periods; also note hourly shape if useful)",
  "criteria": "1) Use list_metrics to discover which models have data for CacheReadInputTokenCount, CacheWriteInputTokenCount, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, and InvocationLatency. 2) For each model with any caching activity, compute 14-day totals (Sum) of cache-read, cache-write, and uncached input tokens; cache hit ratio = cacheRead / (cacheRead + cacheWrite + uncached input); read-to-write ratio; and daily trend (improving / degrading / flat). 3) Estimate cost impact using current published Bedrock pricing for each model (verify pricing via documentation; cache reads are typically heavily discounted vs. base input, cache writes typically carry a premium for some models). Report estimated spend with caching vs. what the same tokens would cost without caching, i.e. net savings (state assumptions and the per-1M-token prices used; if pricing can't be verified, say so and give the token-based figures only). 4) Flag models with high input volume but zero/low cache usage (missed opportunity) and models where cache writes greatly exceed reads (caching costing more than it saves). 5) If no caching metrics exist at all, say so clearly, and report whether Bedrock invocations exist so the user knows caching is simply not in use. Return a concise findings summary with a small per-model table of numbers and a clear verdict; do not dump raw datapoints."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Analyze Bedrock prompt cache metrics in us-east-1 for 14 days"}], "created_at": null}

